Very well if that's the case.

261
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:29,552
I have no choice but to execute
risk prevention procedure.

262
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:43,227
Would you mind at least explaining
why you decided to do this?

263
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:47,097
No, no, no!

264
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:48,239
Let them get away!

265
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:51,000
Ow! My back?

266
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:53,730
No!

267
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:56,170
Julius!

268
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,700
Run, Mar! Run!

269
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,270
I can't!

270
00:16:00,353 --> 00:16:01,860
I can't leave you!

271
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:04,890
Mar!

272
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,830
Julius!

273
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:09,780
It's time for you to stop running.

274
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,717
Is that my father's order?

275
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:14,460
Actually, it's the entire
caravan's decision.

276
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:17,860
Ray, stop!

277
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:18,960
Stop it now!

278
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:22,640
You win.

279
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,060
I'll go back.

280
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,400
But you can't.

281
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,397
We've come this far.

282
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,068
You can't just go back now.

283
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,142
Millie's right.

284
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:30,557
You've got to listen to her.

285
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,934
Don't give up, Julius.

286
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,190
Come on.

287
00:16:34,273 --> 00:16:35,455
It's time to go back.

288
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,360
Oh, Julius.

289
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,720
Ah! Mr. Priest!

290
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,706
Priest, I'm gonna pummel you!

291
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:56,090
More!

292
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:59,120
Lord, what the hell am I doing here?

293
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,840
Thank you so much!

294
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:02,399
I'm glad you came.

295
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:04,324
What made you change your mind?

296
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,470
I don't know.

297
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,637
Guess I was infected by your nosiness.

298
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,014
I think I actually caught it from Vash.

299
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:22,400
Well now, looking for a fight,
then you'd better expect no mercy!

300
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,397
Look, well if it isn't Vash the Stampede?

301
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:54,457
No way was he hired by
my father, please you.

302
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:57,660
Gotta help us, Vash, for
the future of the caravan.

303
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,560
Have you any idea what you're doing?

304
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:16,910
Yep.

305
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:18,493
Your God is my witness.

306
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,150
No!

307
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:42,670
But...

308
00:18:42,753 --> 00:18:43,620
but you shot Julius.

309
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:44,900
It's all over.

310
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,020
Our pass is dead.

311
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:49,199
Hey, it was never part of
the agreement to kill him.

312
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:51,820
Your boss hired me to stop them.

313
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,282
He never mentioned their safety.

314
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,814
I've finished the job.

315
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:00,077
Now leave the money and get lost.

316
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,160
What did you say?

317
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:03,225
Don't do it, are you suicidal?

318
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:06,292
I think we made a big mistake here, guys.

319
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,837
We should never have gone to
someone like him for help.

320
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:12,214
He's just like they said he's
gonna kill us all as well.

321
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,520
Now he's really done it!

322
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,837
How could...

323
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,077
How could...

324
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:27,780
How could he do this?

325
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:33,527
How could you even think of doing
such a horrible, evil thing?

326
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,210
Millie.

327
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,800
Oh, Meryl.

328
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:42,310
Meryl!

329
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:43,977
They're gone.

330
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:45,177
I can't believe it.

331
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,319
He shot them both.

332
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,317
He shot them, Meryl.

333
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,840
I watched them both die!

334
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:57,220
You want to settle what we
started back in May City? Come on!

335
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:03,061
That was a realistic performance.

336
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:06,927
Pretty tough to kill when you're
shooting with rubber bullets.

337
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:14,340
Hey, don't fire those
so close. That stings.

338
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,720
I have a message from your father.

339
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:41,797
He says he's sorry for deceiving you,
and that even though it's no excuse,

340
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:44,657
he only did it because he was
protecting you and the caravan.

341
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:45,570
I understand.

342
00:20:45,653 --> 00:20:47,462
Oh, and there's one other thing.

343
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,520
He asked me to tell you,
you're now free to go.

344
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,090
Father.

345
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:53,490
Julius!

346
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,805
I'm not sure how to thank you.

347
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,480
Don't thank me.

348
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:02,485
He's the one that deserves it.

349
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,880
Hey, you forgot this!

350
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:09,681
Now quickly, you've gotta
go before they spot you.

351
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:10,870
Momma.

352
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:15,077
From this point on, we're gonna go
on living without relying on anyone.

353
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,100
It'll be just the two of us.

354
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:21,500
Well, Millie, you take
care of yourself, okay?

355
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:29,856
And thus, your name is being spread
across the planet even as we speak.

356
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,379
Maybe this is what they call karma.

357
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:35,100
Oh, I don't think so.

358
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,606
She's a good girl, isn't she?

359
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:39,780
She's really good.

360
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,540
Yes, she is.

361
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:45,320
And you, my friend, are just like her.

362
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:51,250
What?

363
00:21:51,333 --> 00:21:53,927
You mean he's really
left for good this time?

364
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:58,020
All of life's journeys come with
meetings and partings and reunions.

365
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,320
I guess that's true.

366
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:03,277
I've got things to do,
so I'll be going now.

367
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,595
Will I see you again?

368
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:05,660
I don't know.

369
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:10,017
And besides, whenever I look at you, I'm
reminded of everything I hate about myself.

370
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,520
You know, it hurts.

371
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:16,480
Nicholas D. Wolfwood.

372
00:22:23,340 --> 00:22:24,580
I'll be darned.

373
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,517
All along, I thought there
had to be a sacrifice.

374
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:29,894
But there was another answer after all.

375
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:31,860
Vash the stampede.

376
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:50,200
The blue sky in the middle of the
sky, the wind is in the future.

377
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:57,120
The light of the day of
the sky, as you can see?

378
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:11,760
Thank you.

379
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:57,037
Thank you so much for watching.

380
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:58,600
No, no, no!

381
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:32,180
Deeper than darkness, Legato Blue
Summers, a man fascinated by death,

382
00:24:32,620 --> 00:24:33,940
only spoke quietly.
